# An sdist must be able to check itself.
#
# Measured 2026-11-19. The wheel and sdist first built from this repository
# carried tests/ but not the data and tools those tests read. Unpacking the sdist
# and running the suite collected 290 of 526 tests, with 6 failures and 97 errors,
# every one of them "no such file". "526 tests green" was true of a git clone and
# false of the package an installer receives.
#
# Fixing it took three passes, measured each time: 290 collected (6F/97E) ->
# 475 collected (13F/57E) -> 482 collected (3F/35E) -> 526 collected, because
# each pass only revealed the next missing directory. The list below is the
# fourth pass, and it grafts every top-level directory a test can read rather
# than guessing which ones matter.

include README.md LICENSE NOTICE NOTICE.md CITATION.cff CITATION.bib codemeta.json
# The register is part of what the package says about itself, and a test reads it
# from the archive. Shipping tests/ without the file a test opens is the same
# failure class as the .github gap that made main red between #288 and #294.
include REPRODUCTION-REGISTER.md

graft uibc_core
graft tests
graft fixtures
graft tools
graft conformance
graft examples
graft adapters
graft ai
graft anchors
graft benchmark
graft brand
graft contest
graft deploy
graft docs
graft drafts
graft evidence
graft failure_corpus
graft independent_verifier
graft lgd-core
graft mcp_server
graft paper
graft registry
graft registry_server
graft timestamps

# Built output and byte-code never belong in a source distribution.
prune tools/out
prune build
prune dist
prune uibc_core.egg-info
global-exclude __pycache__
global-exclude *.pyc
